    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 70.866, 572.602, 524.41, 618.43 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Resultants and subresultants are the algebraic tools used to determine both the projection of the intersection curve between the considered surfaces and its lifting from the plane to the 3D space, because they provide a very easy and compact way of characterizing the greatest common divisor of two polynomials when they involve parameters."
  }, {
